From: Local integration <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: complete selected stopped-tick backports for OEM 6.6.89

Apply only after the accepted 21-patch Crystal/LZ4KDS/le9uo profile.
The earlier squash imported upstream safe-timer additions but retained two
older guards that override their intended selection behavior.

Menu: query timers whenever the tick is stopped, and remove the obsolete
prediction override while preserving the existing non-stopped iowait-based
latency adjustment.  This completes the selected upstream changes:
80606f4eb8d7484ab7f7d6f0fd30d71e6fbcf328 (always check stopped-tick timers)
e57c2bf2e89df3b176ab579abfd3ed54fd27034c (safe timer range).

TEO: let the real timer deadline clamp the candidate without the previous
minimum-one-tick veto, as required by
106a2662e655363db0dd73d9a91e1ec9afe9f4b1 (rearrange stopped-tick handling).
Keep the OEM utilization policy, exported threshold APIs, no-poll helper,
and the separate util-policy guard.  Do not replace either whole governor,
change a global ABI layout, or select a different runtime governor.

---
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/governors/menu.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/governors/menu.c
@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@
 
 	/* Find the shortest expected idle interval. */
 	predicted_ns = get_typical_interval(data) * NSEC_PER_USEC;
-	if (predicted_ns > RESIDENCY_THRESHOLD_NS) {
+	if (predicted_ns > RESIDENCY_THRESHOLD_NS || tick_nohz_tick_stopped()) {
 		unsigned int timer_us;
 
 		/* Determine the time till the closest timer. */
@@ -337,18 +337,7 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (tick_nohz_tick_stopped()) {
-		/*
-		 * If the tick is already stopped, the cost of possible short
-		 * idle duration misprediction is much higher, because the CPU
-		 * may be stuck in a shallow idle state for a long time as a
-		 * result of it.  In that case say we might mispredict and use
-		 * the known time till the closest timer event for the idle
-		 * state selection.
-		 */
-		if (predicted_ns < TICK_NSEC)
-			predicted_ns = data->next_timer_ns;
-	} else {
+	if (!tick_nohz_tick_stopped()) {
 		/*
 		 * Use the performance multiplier and the user-configurable
 		 * latency_req to determine the maximum exit latency.
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/governors/teo.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/governors/teo.c
@@ -601,11 +601,8 @@
 	 * If the closest expected timer is before the target residency of the
 	 * candidate state, a shallower one needs to be found.
 	 */
-	if (drv->states[idx].target_residency_ns > duration_ns) {
-		i = teo_find_shallower_state(drv, dev, idx, duration_ns, false);
-		if (teo_state_ok(i, drv))
-			idx = i;
-	}
+	if (drv->states[idx].target_residency_ns > duration_ns)
+		idx = teo_find_shallower_state(drv, dev, idx, duration_ns, false);
 
 	/*
 	 * If the selected state's target residency is below the tick length
